From a815b31a31e860dc237a9c5788fea171d3448b6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:23:28 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] ci(macos): let the three room-mini runners serve the macOS
 lanes [daveey]

Operator note (2026-11-14): keep the macOS runners on custom runners and use all
three Mac minis. The office minis a, b and c now each run a
dedicated example-org/hermes runner as the hidden non-GUI ci
user (LaunchDaemon, nice 19 + low-priority I/O, /Users/ci/actions-runner-hermes).

Two things pinned the lanes to the mini's runner:
- hermes_state (macOS)'s first step refused every runner root except
  /Users/me/ci-runner-hermes-state, so a job on a room mini would fail
  before checkout. It now selects its root from a two-entry allowlist by
  RUNNER_TEMP and keeps every other guard.
- recover_macos_runner.py reran a runner-lost job only on mini-hermes-state-1.
  It now accepts the four dedicated runner names (RUNNER_NAMES); a non-str
  runner name is refused instead of raising.

Runner labels decide which hosts take jobs, so no runs-on changes. Comments
that described "the one mini runner" now describe the pool.

Tests (Mac, hermes-core-wt test --local, 0 skips): checkout retention 32,
recover 67, macos-os workflow 26. Predictions written first. Mutants killed:
cleanup ignoring the RUNNER_TEMP selection (1 fail), recover back to the
single name (3 fail), runner-name check removed (4 fail), str guard dropped
(1 fail). Equivalent: falling back to the first root when none matches (the
expected-environment RUNNER_TEMP equality refuses the same inputs).
